      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="who-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="who-h">Who it’s for</h2>
        <h3 class="ent-h">Your two-person ops team works like ten.</h3>
        <p class="ent-body">Work is being reorganized around AI, and growing companies feel it first. They need revenue ops, finance, planning and supply chain running well long before they can staff a full team for each, while their people already use AI on their own, scattered across a dozen tools with no one steering it.</p>
        <p class="ent-body">OpenShore brings it into one place. Your team and expert bots share the same chats and projects. You message a bot like an employee, it does the work with sources, and a person approves every change. It runs on whatever models the company already uses, on its own keys.</p>
        <p class="ent-body">Our bet is that every company will soon divide its work between people and agents. Startups can build that way from day one, so we start there and grow with them.</p>
        <p class="ent-body">Bots and agents aren’t the same thing. Bots are the experts we set up for each function. Agents are what your people and your bots start to get the work done. <a href="/enterprise/platform/">The product tour</a> shows both at work.</p>
        <p class="ent-statement">Every Team — Every Agent. Working as One.</p>
      </section>

